# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (docker-compose bind-mounts them from the host
# filesystem as-is — see docker-compose.yml's `mihomes`/`postgres` services). A CRLF shebang or
# CRLF-terminated lines break `sh` on the container side; on a Windows checkout with the common
# core.autocrlf=true, a plain `*.sh` file gets silently corrupted to CRLF on checkout otherwise.
# `eol=lf` pins the working-tree line ending regardless of the cloning machine's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
